<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en-AU">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="/images/favicon.png" />
    <title>Terms of Service | Intelligent Talent Matching Platform</title>
    <meta name="description" content="TalentMatch helps candidates find jobs and employers find candidates using intelligent profile and job matching." />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/lib/css/font-awesome.min.css" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/lib/css/modern-normalize.min.css" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/global.css" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/policy.css" />
    <script data-cfasync="false" src="/lib/js/jquery.min.js"></script>
</head>
<body class="<%= theme === 'DARK' ? 'dark-mode' : '' %>">
<%- include('../partials/public-header/public-header'); %>
<main class="policy-page">
    <section class="policy-page__hero" aria-labelledby="terms-title">
        <div class="policy-page__hero-inner">
            <p class="policy-page__eyebrow">
                Legal
            </p>
            <h1 id="terms-title" class="policy-page__title">
                Terms of Service
            </h1>
            <p class="policy-page__intro">
                These Terms of Service govern your access to and use of TalentMatch,
                including candidate accounts, employer accounts, job postings,
                recommendations, applications, memberships, and related platform functionality.
            </p>
            <p class="policy-page__updated">
                Last updated: 31 May 2026
            </p>
        </div>
    </section>
    <section class="policy-page__layout" aria-label="Terms of service content">
        <aside class="policy-page__sidebar" aria-label="Terms of service sections">
            <nav class="policy-page__nav">
                <a class="policy-page__nav-link" href="#acceptance">Acceptance</a>
                <a class="policy-page__nav-link" href="#eligibility">Eligibility</a>
                <a class="policy-page__nav-link" href="#accounts">Accounts</a>
                <a class="policy-page__nav-link" href="#candidate-responsibilities">Candidates</a>
                <a class="policy-page__nav-link" href="#employer-responsibilities">Employers</a>
                <a class="policy-page__nav-link" href="#recommendations">Recommendations</a>
                <a class="policy-page__nav-link" href="#membership">Membership</a>
                <a class="policy-page__nav-link" href="#acceptable-use">Acceptable Use</a>
                <a class="policy-page__nav-link" href="#intellectual-property">Intellectual Property</a>
                <a class="policy-page__nav-link" href="#availability">Availability</a>
                <a class="policy-page__nav-link" href="#liability">Liability</a>
                <a class="policy-page__nav-link" href="#termination">Termination</a>
                <a class="policy-page__nav-link" href="#changes">Changes</a>
                <a class="policy-page__nav-link" href="#contact">Contact</a>
            </nav>
        </aside>
        <article class="policy-page__content">
            <section id="acceptance" class="policy-page__section">
                <h2 class="policy-page__section-title"> 1. Acceptance of Terms </h2>
                <p class="policy-page__paragraph"> By accessing or using TalentMatch, you agree to comply with these Terms of Service. If you do not agree with these Terms, you must not access or use the platform. </p>
                <p class="policy-page__paragraph"> These Terms apply to all users of the Intelligent Talent Matching Platform, including candidates, employers, visitors, and administrators. </p>
            </section>
            <section id="eligibility" class="policy-page__section">
                <h2 class="policy-page__section-title"> 2. Eligibility </h2>
                <p class="policy-page__paragraph"> Users must be at least 18 years old or otherwise legally capable of entering into binding agreements under applicable law. </p>
                <p class="policy-page__paragraph"> You are responsible for ensuring that all information provided to TalentMatch is accurate, complete, and current. </p>
            </section>
            <section id="accounts" class="policy-page__section">
                <h2 class="policy-page__section-title"> 3. User Accounts </h2>
                <p class="policy-page__paragraph"> Users may create candidate or employer accounts to access platform functionality. You are responsible for maintaining the confidentiality of your account credentials. </p>
                <p class="policy-page__paragraph"> You are responsible for all activity performed through your account unless otherwise required by law. </p>
            </section>
            <section id="candidate-responsibilities" class="policy-page__section">
                <h2 class="policy-page__section-title"> 4. Candidate Responsibilities </h2>
                <p class="policy-page__paragraph"> Candidates are responsible for ensuring that profile information, qualifications, certifications, skills, experience, and resumes are truthful and accurate. </p>
                <p class="policy-page__paragraph"> Providing false, misleading, or fraudulent information may result in account suspension or removal. </p>
            </section>
            <section id="employer-responsibilities" class="policy-page__section">
                <h2 class="policy-page__section-title"> 5. Employer Responsibilities </h2>
                <p class="policy-page__paragraph"> Employers are responsible for ensuring that job postings, company information, salary details, and recruitment activities are lawful, accurate, and not misleading. </p>
                <p class="policy-page__paragraph"> Employers must comply with all applicable employment, discrimination, privacy, and workplace laws. </p>
            </section>
            <section id="recommendations" class="policy-page__section">
                <h2 class="policy-page__section-title"> 6. Recommendations and Matching </h2>
                <p class="policy-page__paragraph"> TalentMatch provides recommendation and matching features intended to assist candidates and employers in discovering relevant opportunities and profiles. </p>
                <p class="policy-page__paragraph"> Recommendation scores, rankings, and suitability indicators are informational only and should not be considered hiring, recruitment, legal, or professional advice. </p>
                <p class="policy-page__paragraph"> TalentMatch does not guarantee employment outcomes, interview opportunities, hiring decisions, or recruitment success. </p>
            </section>
            <section id="membership" class="policy-page__section">
                <h2 class="policy-page__section-title"> 7. Membership Services </h2>
                <p class="policy-page__paragraph"> Certain features may be limited to membership plans or premium services. Membership benefits and limits may change over time. </p>
                <p class="policy-page__paragraph"> Any paid memberships or subscription services will be governed by the pricing and billing information provided at the time of purchase. </p>
            </section>
            <section id="acceptable-use" class="policy-page__section">
                <h2 class="policy-page__section-title"> 8. Acceptable Use </h2>
                <p class="policy-page__paragraph"> Users must not: </p>
                <ul class="policy-page__list">
                    <li class="policy-page__list-item">Provide false or misleading information.</li>
                    <li class="policy-page__list-item">Attempt to gain unauthorized access to accounts or systems.</li>
                    <li class="policy-page__list-item">Upload malicious software or harmful content.</li>
                    <li class="policy-page__list-item">Scrape, harvest, or bulk extract platform data.</li>
                    <li class="policy-page__list-item">Use the platform for unlawful activities.</li>
                    <li class="policy-page__list-item">Interfere with platform security or availability.</li>
                </ul>
            </section>
            <section id="intellectual-property" class="policy-page__section">
                <h2 class="policy-page__section-title"> 9. Intellectual Property </h2>
                <p class="policy-page__paragraph"> TalentMatch, including its branding, software, interfaces, recommendation systems, and platform content, remains the property of TalentMatch or its licensors. </p>
                <p class="policy-page__paragraph"> Users retain ownership of information they submit but grant TalentMatch permission to process and display that information for platform operation and recommendation functionality. </p>
            </section>
            <section id="availability" class="policy-page__section">
                <h2 class="policy-page__section-title"> 10. Service Availability </h2>
                <p class="policy-page__paragraph"> TalentMatch aims to provide reliable service but does not guarantee uninterrupted access, continuous availability, or error-free operation. </p>
                <p class="policy-page__paragraph"> Platform functionality may be modified, suspended, or discontinued where reasonably necessary. </p>
            </section>
            <section id="liability" class="policy-page__section">
                <h2 class="policy-page__section-title"> 11. Limitation of Liability </h2>
                <p class="policy-page__paragraph"> To the maximum extent permitted by law, TalentMatch is not liable for indirect, incidental, consequential, special, or economic losses arising from use of the platform. </p>
                <p class="policy-page__paragraph"> Users remain responsible for evaluating employment opportunities, candidate suitability, and recruitment outcomes. </p>
            </section>
            <section id="termination" class="policy-page__section">
                <h2 class="policy-page__section-title"> 12. Suspension and Termination </h2>
                <p class="policy-page__paragraph"> TalentMatch may suspend or terminate access where users breach these Terms, compromise platform security, or engage in unlawful or harmful conduct. </p>
            </section>
            <section id="changes" class="policy-page__section">
                <h2 class="policy-page__section-title"> 13. Changes to These Terms </h2>
                <p class="policy-page__paragraph"> These Terms may be updated periodically. Continued use of TalentMatch after changes are published constitutes acceptance of the updated Terms. </p>
            </section>
            <section id="contact" class="policy-page__section">
                <h2 class="policy-page__section-title"> 14. Contact </h2>
                <p class="policy-page__paragraph"> Questions regarding these Terms may be directed to: </p>
                <p class="policy-page__paragraph"> <a class="policy-page__inline-link" href="mailto:support@talentmatch.com"> support@talentmatch.com </a> </p>
            </section>
            <section class="policy-page__note" aria-label="Important note">
                <h2 class="policy-page__note-title">
                    Academic Project Disclaimer
                </h2>
                <p class="policy-page__paragraph">
                    TalentMatch and all associated policies, terms, and documentation have been
                    developed as part of CSIT314 – Software Development Methodologies at the
                    University of Wollongong for academic assessment purposes. These documents
                    have not been reviewed by legal professionals and are not intended to
                    constitute legal advice or create legally binding obligations. Any future
                    production or commercial deployment should be subject to independent legal,
                    privacy, and regulatory review.
                </p>
            </section>
        </article>
    </section>
</main>
<%- include('../partials/footer/footer'); %>
<script data-cfasync="false" src="/js/global.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
